# VS Code packaging policy for this extension.
#
# Shipped: the generated entry points (client/extension.cjs, server/server.js),
# the manifest, docs, icon, and licenses (including the generated
# licenses/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md), and only the server bundle's external
# runtime dependency closure (@designlasagna/schemas). ajv, ajv-formats,
# jsonc-parser, and the client's vscode-languageclient closure are compiled
# into the generated bundles, so nothing of theirs ships from node_modules.
#
# scripts/validate-package.mjs derives that closure from the bundle-server
# build script and the lockfile and verifies the packaged archive against it,
# so nothing here is keyed off a package's name alone.
#
# Everything under node_modules is excluded by default; each retained file
# below is negated explicitly.

node_modules/

# @designlasagna/schemas (MIT): only the six documents the server loads
# (including the lifecycle schema the v0.4 documents $ref) plus its license
# and manifest.
!node_modules/@designlasagna/schemas/package.json
!node_modules/@designlasagna/schemas/LICENSE
!node_modules/@designlasagna/schemas/v0.3/tokens.json
!node_modules/@designlasagna/schemas/v0.3/dtcg-extensions.json
!node_modules/@designlasagna/schemas/v0.4/tokens.json
!node_modules/@designlasagna/schemas/v0.4/lifecycle.json
!node_modules/@designlasagna/schemas/v0.4/dtcg-extensions.json
!node_modules/@designlasagna/schemas/dtcg/2025.10/format.json

# Editable client source, tooling, and docs that are never shipped.
.gitignore
extension.js
scripts/**
SETUP.md
icon.svg
